## Behavioural notes

- Files are identified by source plus relative path; `/file/Pi/workflow.md` and `/file/Claude/workflow.md` are distinct documents and never share content.
- Return contexts are kept per document URL for the page session, so Back/Forward chains restore the right browsing state; direct links and reloads fall back to the containing folder with ancestors revealed.
- Request lifecycle: each fetch is tied to the document identity and attempt and aborted when the location changes, so stale successes and errors are dropped.
- The API decodes the query once; the client decodes each URL segment once; `%252e%252e` therefore names a literal (absent) file rather than a parent directory.

## Known limitations

- Vite's dev server answers 404 for URLs with malformed percent-encoding before the SPA loads, so the invalid-link state for malformed encoding is reachable only through in-app history (tested that way with `pushState` + `popstate`). Well-formed but invalid links (unknown source, server-rejected path) are covered end to end.
- YAML frontmatter is rendered as ordinary Markdown on the Rendered tab (a rule followed by a setext heading), as `react-markdown` does without a frontmatter plugin. The Source tab shows it verbatim, as required.
- Only `https:` images load; `http:` images show the unavailable placeholder alongside relative images. Relative images and an asset route remain deferred per the PRD.
- Graph layout, pan/zoom and outline scroll are restored within a page session only; they are not persisted across reloads (not required).
- The `hash` is exposed on the document view as a `data-hash` attribute for tests and future use; it is not displayed.
